# insulate: heat-shrink sleeving (decision C20). The resistor's lead 1
# will run along the chip's pin row to pin 3, past pins 2 and 1. First
# the resistor goes in the vise; the sleeve station S6 slides a sleeve
# onto lead 1 from its free end, 4 to 11 mm from the body, and shrinks
# it with hot air; the resistor goes back to the tray. Then the chip goes
# in the vise legs up; the rig bends lead 1 12 mm from the body and
# shears it to a 4 mm end, and the arm lays that end alongside pin 3's
# leg (a lap joint, decision C22). The bent end is longer than the lap,
# so the sleeved lead passes over pins 2 and 1, clear of them, insulated
# all the same; then it is soldered.
reset circuit=lap
tool A tweezers
pick A R1 grasp=body
place A R1 at=0,0,-20
vise close
release A R1
lift A mm=60
present R1.1.tip at=S6
sleeve S6 on=R1.1 from=4 to=11 size=1.0 color=blue
present R1.1.8 at=S6
shrink S6 on=R1.1
stage to=0 tilt=0 at=0,0,0
pick A R1 grasp=body
vise open
lift A mm=60
place A R1 at=222.749,194.464,-138.35 rpy=0,0,90
release A R1
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=180,0,90
vise close
release A U1
pick A R1 grasp=body
lift A mm=60
insert A on=R1.1 at=12
form angle=90
lift A mm=30
shear A on=R1.1 at=17.2
lift A mm=60
bring A R1.1 to=U1.3.tip along=0,-1,0 lap=3.2 from=0,0,1
pinch P2 on=R1.1 at=3
release A R1
lift A mm=60
inspect shorts
present U1.3+R1.1 at=S1
scope aim=U1.3+R1.1 zoom=8
touch S1 at=U1.3+R1.1 dwell=2
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.3+R1.1 below=100
inspect U1.3+R1.1
unpinch P2
inspect shorts
